$$SYNTAX-LEVEL 2
*(about
  <a href="#" class="drop">$(about_name)</a>
  <span id="about_menu">
    <div class="dropdown_5columns mega-dropdown mega-dropdown-about">
      <div class="mega-panel-heading mega-panel-heading-row">
        <div class="mega-heading-text">
          <!-- Fits on one line at the panel's 560px: the string measures 361px
               at the h2's 19px/700, against 396px left beside the action. Both
               numbers move if the panel narrows or the action's label grows.
               The .mega-heading-text wrapper is flex:1 1 auto / min-width:0, so
               it hands the h2 the same width it had before the hint arrived. -->
          <h2>Maize Genetics and Genomics Database</h2>
          <!-- The same one-line hint the Tools and Data Hubs panels carry:
               filled in by mgdb-chrome.js from the pointed-at link's data-desc,
               and reset to the default below once the pointer or focus leaves
               the grid. It replaces the "Project" and "Learn" group headings,
               which named categories rather than saying what anything was.
               aria-hidden because it is a pointer affordance duplicating the
               link the reader is already on; screen readers get the label. -->
          <p class="mega-hint" data-mgdb-hint data-mgdb-hint-default="Point at a link to see what it covers." aria-hidden="true">Point at a link to see what it covers.</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Same shape as the Genomes panel: no eyebrow, no footer, and the
             section destination sits here beside the heading. The site map is
             that destination rather than /about, which is a page about the
             project rather than a way into the rest of the site. -->
        <div class="mega-heading-actions">
          <a class="mega-heading-action" href="$(server-url)/sitemap">Explore site map <span aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mega-grid mega-grid-2 mega-compact-groups">
        <!-- No group headings. Four links do not need to be sorted into
             "Project" and "Learn", and those two words described the shelf
             rather than what was on it; the hover description in the heading
             does the work instead. Divs rather than sections, because a
             <section> with no heading has no accessible name. The two-column
             split is kept so the panel keeps its shape above the affiliation
             row. Descriptions use the site map's wording where the site map
             has one, so a destination reads the same in both places; /contact
             and /cite carry no site map description, so theirs are drawn from
             the pages' own opening lines. -->
        <div class="mega-group">
          <a href="$(server-url)/contact" data-desc="Questions about data, tools, curation, or the site itself, and who to ask."><strong>People &amp; contact</strong></a>
          <a href="$(server-url)/cite" data-desc="The current reference for MaizeGDB, and how to cite it."><strong>Cite MaizeGDB</strong></a>
        </div>
        <!-- "Documentation" pointed at /doc, a legacy page of ten links of
             which four were dead or aimed at the wrong target, and the word
             itself read as documentation of the website rather than of the
             research projects the page was for. /projects is that directory
             now; /doc redirects to it. -->
        <div class="mega-group">
          <a href="$(server-url)/projects" data-desc="Every maize research project with data, results, or documentation here."><strong>Research projects</strong></a>
          <a href="$(server-url)/whatsnew" data-desc="MaizeGDB news, by year, back to 2007."><strong>News &amp; updates</strong></a>
        </div>
        <!-- The membership was a full feature column, which gave a partner
             organization the same weight as MaizeGDB's own sections. It is an
             affiliation, so it reads as one: a single row across the foot of
             the grid, carrying AgBioData's own agriculture mark. "Founding
             member" is the site's existing wording, used verbatim in the
             footer of every unmodernized page.
             The whole row is one link, so it is one tap target in the drawer. -->
        <a class="mega-affiliation" href="https://www.agbiodata.org" data-desc="AgBioData: the consortium making agricultural research data findable, accessible, interoperable and reusable." target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <img class="mega-affiliation-mark" src="$(image-dir)/quicklinks/agbiodata.png" alt="" width="128" height="128" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <span class="mega-affiliation-text">
            <strong>Founding member of AgBioData</strong>
            <span>The consortium making agricultural research data findable, accessible, interoperable, and reusable.</span>
          </span>
          <span class="mega-affiliation-cue" aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </span>
)
